    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50252" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱκετ-εία</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῐ], ἡ</span>, more 
			Att.
		 form of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱκεσία</span> (q.v.),
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>supplication</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				1.24
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱκετείαν ποιεῖσθαί
			τινος</span> to supplicate him, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				3.67
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱκετεῖαι θεῶν</span>
			<i>addressed to</i> them, <i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				2.39
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐφ᾽ ἱκετείαν τραπόμενος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Ap.</u>
					39a
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μετὰ δεήσεως καὶ ἱ</span>.
				<i><span class="en">
				<u>PPetr.</u>
				2p.60
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				1181.12
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Jewish</span>): pl., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-είας ποιεῖσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Smp.</u>
					183a
				</span></i>
			, etc.</div>
